From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] opengl32: wglGetLayerPaletteEntries (3596)

opengl32: wglGetLayerPaletteEntries

The pixel formats have no layer planes, so there is no palette to read:
the function returns 0 without complaining.
---
diff --git a/dlls/opengl32/wgl.c b/dlls/opengl32/wgl.c
index 5a527ad..5841b78 100644
--- a/dlls/opengl32/wgl.c
+++ b/dlls/opengl32/wgl.c
@@ -970,7 +970,8 @@ BOOL WINAPI wglDescribeLayerPlane(HDC hdc,
  */
 int WINAPI wglGetLayerPaletteEntries( HDC hdc, int plane, int start, int count, COLORREF *colors )
 {
-    FIXME( "hdc %p, plane %d, start %d, count %d, colors %p, stub!\n", hdc, plane, start, count, colors );
+    TRACE( "hdc %p, plane %d, start %d, count %d, colors %p.\n", hdc, plane, start, count, colors );
+    /* the pixel formats have no layer planes, so there is no palette to read */
     return 0;
 }
 
